# Laying out a page

Every tool's page has one layout, the same on its front page and its item pages and the same from tool to tool: switching screens moves nothing. tools-common's page kit (`localweb/page`) draws it, and `PAGE-STANDARD.md` in tools-common holds the rules. Use the kit's parts for every place below. A page that needs something they don't give gets a change to the kit, not CSS of its own.

## The page and its places

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ bar (52px): brand · sections · status            also · live · Guide · ▣  │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ band (104px at every width)                                              │
│  title · beside · fold                        end · search · ⋯           │  title line
│  under: stage track, or status pills          underEnd · group · sort    │  second line
├────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────┤
│ left 288px │ middle                                    │ right           │
│ first label│ first card 24px under the band            │ thread, or tabs │
│ 16px under │ cards: 14px by 16px padding, 8px corner,  │ with counts;    │
│ the band   │ up to 1100px, left-aligned                │ first label 16px│
│            │                                           │ under the band  │
└────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────┘
```

| Place | What goes there | Kit part |
|---|---|---|
| Bar | Brand, the tool's sections, status, other open work, live, Guide, theme, one primary action on the far right; on a hosted machine it starts with the workspace's name (a link to billet's start page) and the diazo \| cast \| galley switch with the current tool filled in, neither on a device | `bar` |
| Band | The page's title strip, 104px at every width, a phone included, with or without its second line | `band` |
| Title line | The title, then `beside` (its place, its state), then `fold` (beside nodes that go into the ⋯ on a phone, and on any width where the title would go under 320px beside them; an entry with `shrink` gives way first, with an ellipsis) | `band`'s `title`, `beside`, `fold` |
| Title line's end | `fold` entries with `at: 'end'` (actions that go into the ⋯ on a phone, as galley's History), then `end` (the page's actions), then `search` (a front page's search field, 240px when there is room), then the one ⋯ (`menu`, and the fold's items on a phone) | `band`'s `fold`, `end`, `search`, `menu` |
| Second line | The stage track on an item page, the status pills on a front page; one line that scrolls sideways when too long | `band`'s `under`, with `stageTrack` or `statusPills` |
| Second line's end | `underEnd` (the needs-you pill on an item page), then a front page's group switch when its list offers several groupings (none, project, status; one may be by a left-column filter, since the reader chooses it), then `sort` (a front page's sort: recent, stage, name; "sort in groups" while grouped); each a compact picker on a phone | `band`'s `underEnd`, `sortedList`'s `band` and `groupings` |
| Left column | 288px; its first label 16px under the band; its sections are the page's own (filters on a front page, an index on an item page) | `frame`'s `left`, `indexSection`, `filterRow` |
| Middle column | Its first card 24px under the band; every card 14px by 16px padding, an 8px corner, up to 1100px, left-aligned (the empty-state card, `emptyCard`, keeps its own padding). A list whose rows can be picked several at a time has the kit's tick boxes, on each row and on each group's head (or the card's head); the actions on what is picked go in the band | `frame`'s `centre`, `card`, `emptyCard`, `sortedList` (`pick` for the tick boxes) |
| Right column | An item page's thread, or its tabs with counts; its first label 16px under the band | `frame`'s `right`, `thread`, `railTabs` |
| Phone (640px wide or less) | On a phone the bar stays one 52px line: the switch, the brand, the sections and the primary stay, and the workspace's name, the status, other open work, live, Guide and theme go into the bar's ⋯. The band stays 104px and the title stays whole while the rest of its line gives way (what is beside it, then the search down to 96px); the fold goes into the band's ⋯. The columns follow the kit's three layouts: at 999px or less one column shows at a time; from 1000px to 1319px two, the middle with one side open beside it (the right on an item page, the left on a front page) and the other a 44px strip; from 1320px all three. A width rule of a tool's own is built from `KIT_WIDTHS`. On a touch screen strips and column toggles take a 44px press | `bar`, `band`, `narrowMode`, `KIT_WIDTHS` |

A front page has no right column: leave `right` out of `frame` and its middle runs to the window's edge, its cards still stopping at 1100px. The one wide view, a system design's topic chat, runs the middle over the right column's space with `frame`'s `wide`; the band, the left column and the middle's left edge stay where they are.

## What never goes where

- Nothing goes between the band and the columns: no search box, sort line, notice or toolbar over the cards.
- Search and sort go only through the band: `band`'s `search`, and `sortedList` given the band. A list never draws its own sort over its cards.
- Actions on picked rows go in the band, never in a toolbar or button row over the list: the main one a `fold` entry with `at: 'end'` at the title line's end (on a phone it moves into the ⋯), the rest in the band's one ⋯, each label counting the picked rows showing.
- No tool CSS for the band's height, the columns' widths or start, or the cards' padding, corner or 1100px cap. The kit sets them; a tool's own rules for them are removed when it adopts the kit's layout.
- One ⋯ in the band, the kit's: give it items with `menu`, never a second button of the tool's own.
- What the places hold (a page's stages, its left rows, its cards' contents, its ⋯ items) is the tool's own; where they go is not.

## Mockups

Start every mockup from the mockup starter, served with the kit at `/_kit/layout/` on any tool's page server: the bar, the band and the three columns drawn with the kit's own stylesheet and classes, each place labelled, as a front page and an item page, at desktop and phone width. Copy it, replace each labelled place with what the screen holds, and keep the kit's stylesheet: a mockup that sets its own sizes for the band, the columns or the cards has drifted from the page it shows.

## Checking a page

Load the tool's front page and an item page in a headless browser at 1655px, 1280px, 1180px, 1032px and 390px wide, and compare: the bar, the band (104px) and the left column are the same; each column's first label and first card start at the same left edge and top; from 1820px up the first card is 1100px wide on both. At 1180px and 1032px (two columns) an item page has its right column open and its left a strip, a front page its left open, nothing scrolls sideways, and the first card is at least 550px wide. Then switch between the pages and see nothing jump.
